{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788306397,"nonce":"l4djuWruffIsJ+0qb2NrM1xn494=","title":"'Armoured' is unreadable: apparel rows carry no armor rating, so a militia's protection cannot be graded","message":"Found while rewriting `664e9b9` (the M1 re-run). Evan's militia is \"armed, armoured, posture set, able to survive a raid\". Three of the four are readable today — armed from `pawn {sections:[\"equipment\"]}` (`primary`), posture from `digest.posture`, survival from the journal. **Armoured is not.**\n\n`PawnSerializer.Apparel` publishes per item `def`, `label`, `quality`, `hp_pct` and the pawn rollup `worst_hp_pct`, `worst_wear`, `comfort_min_c`/`comfort_max_c`. `grep -n \"Armor\" Source/AutoRimmer/PawnSerializer.cs` returns nothing. So \"is this colonist armoured\" can only be answered today by a def-name list (FlakVest, FlakJacket, PlateArmor, SimpleHelmet ...) — a list that goes stale on the first modded armour and that calls a devilstrand duster unarmoured.\n\n**The game's number.** Armour is per item and per body part: `RimWorld/ArmorUtility.GetPostArmorDamage` walks `pawn.apparel.WornApparel` and reads `apparel.GetStatValue(armorRatingStat)` for the layer covering the struck part — `StatDefOf.ArmorRating_Sharp` / `ArmorRating_Blunt` / `ArmorRating_Heat`. `PawnSerializer` already reads pawn stats through `GetStatValue` (`ComfyTemperatureMax`), so the route is established; what is new is reading it on the apparel Thing and saying which parts it covers.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Each `apparel` row carries `armor_sharp`, `armor_blunt`, `armor_heat` (as the game would apply them — quality and HP included) and the body-part groups the item covers.\n- A per-pawn rollup shaped by what `ArmorUtility.GetPostArmorDamage` actually consults: best sharp/blunt rating over the torso and head groups at minimum. The exact shape is the implementer's investigation, cited by member.\n- NO invented `armoured` verdict unless a threshold is defended from source; publish the numbers and let the reader decide.\n- Sibling of `c41bdcc` (weapons). If both land, one `defence` section is the natural home — decide there, not here.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A colonist wearing a flak vest reads a torso sharp rating equal to the game's own inspect-pane value for that item; `drop` it and the rollup falls to the natural (0) value. Both measured on a bench.\n- No accessor adopted mutates on read (2.4's save-diff method); `StatWorker` caching on apparel is checked and cited.\n- Cheap on session 19's axis or measured and justified.\n- `664e9b9`'s militia row upgrades \"armoured\" from narrative to graded only after this ships; the contract says so.","files":null}]}